      <activity id="d883fa6a-3866-5457-b44f-e9f182536461" activityNameId="daa1309c-0b77-58d6-a19c-6e05680d785b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ground heat exchanger for office buildings, short: 0.267 m</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ground heat exchanger for office buildings, short: 0.267 m
Disposal of a ground heat exchanger for an office building with a specific air flow rate of 4.0 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on a short ground heat exchanger with a specific duct lenght of 0.067m per m3 nominal air flow. The inventory includes a ground heat exchanger with 200mm diameter and a lenght of 0.267m/m2. The data represents a ground heat exchanger made of polyethylene. It includes the excavating needed and a bedding layer made of poor concrete.;
UUID: 9997100c-5ee6-434d-9c98-d99d9d3ec196
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Process information partly from 2008. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9997100c-5ee6-434d-9c98-d99d9d3ec196.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
